# Title: Regsvr32 DLL Execution With Uncommon Extension
# ID: 50919691-7302-437f-8e10-1fe088afa145
# Status: test
# Level: medium
# Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
# Date: 2019-07-17
# Tags: attack.privilege-escalation, attack.persistence, attack.stealth, attack.t1574, attack.execution
# Description: Detects a "regsvr32" execution where the DLL doesn't contain a common file extension.
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

index=* eventtype=wineventlog (((process_path="*\\regsvr32.exe") OR (process_name="REGSVR32.EXE")) AND NOT (((process_exec="") OR ((process_exec="*.ax*" OR process_exec="*.cpl*" OR process_exec="*.dll*" OR process_exec="*.ocx*")) OR (NOT process_exec=*))) AND NOT (((process_exec="*.bav*") OR (process_exec="*.ppl*"))))
